The proposal's napari facts S2–S4 are complete source captures of `napari/docs@main`, a moving development branch captured 2026-10-05. **[FACT S17–S19]** A retrieval scoped to that same dependency found napari v0.9.2 published 2026-09-29; the `v0.9.2` git ref resolves to commit `595639295a153c84bcb127a9e07d801355440a35`. Its release notes say RGB data can now be viewed in 3D, while warning that the feature may still have issues. The current `/stable/` docs index identifies doc version 0.9.2. This is a coherent release anchor for the RGB-in-3D statement, not proof that every detailed `main`-branch image/units/shapes passage is exactly the v0.9.2 behavior. The stable image-page capture was truncated at 524,288 of 1,701,221 bytes; I use its header/version only, not its missing body as evidence. For implementation adoption, use the v0.9.2 source/tests (or a later exact tag) and run V8–V9 against that pin.

